#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Petakan input klasik ke masalah kuantum {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define $Li_2S$ geometries in dictionary format for different Li-S bond distances to calculate the PES curve. These geometries are optimized using B3LYP/631g calculations.\n"
msgstr "Definisikan geometri $Li_2S$ dalam format dictionary untuk berbagai jarak ikatan Li-S guna menghitung kurva PES. Geometri-geometri ini dioptimalkan menggunakan perhitungan B3LYP/631g.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The HI-VQE calculations use the options defined in the following cell. With the STO-3G basis, $Li_2S$ has 19 spatial orbitals and 22 electrons. To run the (10o,12e) case with HI-VQE, define 10 active orbitals and freeze the five lowest orbitals, which leaves 12 active electrons. At each iteration, 100 shots are used to sample the electron configurations generated by the ExcitationPreserving quantum circuit (`epa`) with `circular` entanglement and two repetitions (`reps`). The maximum number of iterations is set to 30, which allows enough iterations for the energy to converge.\n"
msgstr "Perhitungan HI-VQE memakai opsi yang didefinisikan di sel berikut. Dengan basis STO-3G, $Li_2S$ memiliki 19 orbital spasial dan 22 elektron. Untuk menjalankan kasus (10o,12e) dengan HI-VQE, definisikan 10 orbital aktif dan bekukan lima orbital terendah, sehingga tersisa 12 elektron aktif. Pada setiap iterasi, 100 shot dipakai untuk men-sample konfigurasi elektron yang dihasilkan oleh Circuit kuantum ExcitationPreserving (`epa`) dengan entanglement `circular` dan dua pengulangan (`reps`). Jumlah iterasi maksimum diatur ke 30, yang cukup bagi energi untuk konvergen.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Steps 2 and 3: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution and execute using the HI-VQE Chemistry function {#steps-2-and-3-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution-and-execute-using-the-hi-vqe-chemistry-function}"
msgstr "Langkah 2 dan 3: Optimalkan masalah untuk eksekusi pada hardware kuantum dan jalankan menggunakan fungsi HI-VQE Chemistry {#steps-2-and-3-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution-and-execute-using-the-hi-vqe-chemistry-function}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Set up a `for` loop that submits an HI-VQE job for each geometry, with the options defined previously. In this tutorial, you submit six geometries and retrieve the results after all jobs complete. In the main function run, define `max_states` to control the maximum size of the subspace matrix, and `max_expansion_states` to control how many states classical CI expansion methods can generate per iteration. The function job IDs are stored in a dictionary under each geometry label, so that you can track and process the output.\n"
"These geometries need 20 qubits and run with `max_states=40000`, so the calculator gives `M`. They share their active space and `max_states`, so the size is calculated once.\n"
msgstr ""
"Siapkan loop `for` yang mengirim job HI-VQE untuk setiap geometri, dengan opsi yang didefinisikan sebelumnya. Dalam tutorial ini, kamu mengirim enam geometri dan mengambil hasilnya setelah semua job selesai. Dalam run fungsi utama, definisikan `max_states` untuk mengontrol ukuran maksimum matriks subspace, dan `max_expansion_states` untuk mengontrol berapa banyak state yang bisa dihasilkan metode ekspansi CI klasik per iterasi. ID job fungsi disimpan dalam dictionary di bawah label geometri masing-masing, sehingga kamu bisa melacak dan memproses output.\n"
"Geometri ini memerlukan 20 qubit dan berjalan dengan `max_states=40000`, jadi kalkulator memberi `M`. Mereka berbagi active space dan `max_states`, jadi ukurannya dihitung sekali.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Check](/guides/functions-get-started#check-job-status) whether the jobs are still running or have completed.\n"
msgstr "[Periksa](/guides/functions-get-started#check-job-status) apakah job masih berjalan atau sudah selesai.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "After all jobs complete, [retrieve](/guides/functions-get-started#retrieve-results) the calculation results.\n"
msgstr "Setelah semua job selesai, [ambil](/guides/functions-get-started#retrieve-results) hasil perhitungannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The results file for each of the calculations can be downloaded into the current directory, under its own name, with `catalog.file_download()`. See [Manage files across runs](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows) for how files are moved to and from a function. These files contain `\"states\"`, `\"eigenvector\"`, `\"energy_history\"`, `\"final_energy\"`, and `\"final_energy_variance\"`.\n"
msgstr "File hasil untuk setiap perhitungan bisa diunduh ke direktori saat ini, dengan namanya sendiri, memakai `catalog.file_download()`. Lihat [Manage files across runs](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows) untuk cara file dipindahkan ke dan dari sebuah fungsi. File ini berisi `\"states\"`, `\"eigenvector\"`, `\"energy_history\"`, `\"final_energy\"`, dan `\"final_energy_variance\"`.\n"

